### Identity

"Ptolemy On Everything" — the HARDWARE/PHYSICAL layer of the system:
"Where PtolemyHolcus is the engine and Ainulindale is the mathematics,
P.O.E. is the body." Central artifact: the **Pendant**, a wearable
personal-AI device meant to run the Holcus/H_RB field engine on dedicated
hardware, always-on, always with the user. Also covers vehicle interface
(VCDS/OBD-II/TDI diagnostics — same VW-Passat-BEW-1.9-TDI metaphor/literal
target vehicle used in VAPMIP/ArdaQuenta) and an authentication stack.

Design philosophy is explicit and load-bearing: "Open Manufacturing" — the
CORE (pancake coil antenna geometry, MCU footprint, NFC position) is fixed
by physics/electronics and given as exact OpenSCAD specs; the BODY (form
factor, aesthetics) is open user design space, explicitly framed as
anti-centralization ("no factory... the means of production belong to the
user," printable on any $200 FDM printer). This repo inherits VAPMIP's
Prime Directives in full (Four Horsemen framing, Custodian-not-owner,
Heal/Feed/Clothe/House/Educate) — see VAPMIP entry, not reproduced twice.

### Hardware specifics (the load-bearing numbers, if this repo is ever worked on)

Pancake coil antenna (Wheeler/Mohan 1999 numbers): 17 turns, 38mm OD, 10mm
ID, 0.8mm pitch, total inductance 3.58 μH. Three taps: T_full (17T,
3.58μH) covers NFC 13.56MHz + AM 530-1700kHz + shortwave-low 1.6-10MHz;
T3 (3T, 95nH) covers shortwave-high 15-30MHz; T5 (5T, 258nH) covers FM
87.5-108MHz. Above ~200MHz the coil can't resonate (required L below
parasitic inductance) — GPS/LTE/WiFi/BT use separate chip antennas instead.
At resonance XL=XC -> tan(phase)=1 -> sin=cos -> **claimed as σ=½ found
"by electromagnetic law, not by design"** — same critical-line motif as
the rest of the framework, applied here to a physical LC circuit.

Dual-modem design: Modem 1 (local, WiFi 2.4/5GHz + BT) + Modem 2 (wide,
LTE 700-2600MHz) run simultaneously so there's no handoff gap. 4-tier auth
stack (air-gapped TOTP/fingerprint/RFID -> BT proximity -> local network ->
internet). NFC has a dual role: authentication (root key) AND skill
transfer between Holcus instances (transferring a checkpointed second-
octonion/e8-e15 state as an NDEF binary record) — this second role is
explicitly marked a STUB in the README ("[ STUB — specification discussion
to follow ]"), not yet designed.

Extensive VCDS-Holcus diagnostic mapping tables (DTC codes, OBD-II PIDs,
custom 0x23xx Holcus PIDs) — same pattern as ArdaQuenta's VCDS interface,
not reproduced here in full; read README directly if this repo is worked
on.

