### The Nine Reductions (HyperWebster negative-space navigation, summary only)

Presented as a pipeline eliminating unusable regions of the infinite string
address space down to something navigable at fixed cost: (1) Banach-Tarski
equivalence classes over anagrams/permutations, (2) lexical filtering to
natural-language neighborhoods, (3) De Bruijn minimal traversal ordering,
(4) Zipf center-loading (common words get low addresses, Huffman-coding-like),
(5) Horner's bijection itself (string <-> integer, the mathematical core),
(6) octonion splitting (8 limbs of the Horner integer become an 8D
coordinate, so Euclidean proximity in 𝕆 = semantic similarity "by
construction," not computed), (7) the Amplituhedron paradigm (Arkani-Hamed
& Trnka 2013 analogy: replace infinite combinatorial enumeration with one
geometric neighborhood-volume measurement), (8) per-file-type charset
optimization, (9) HYPER_KEY permutation as a cryptographic layer (rotating
the charset permutation rigidly rotates the whole address space; ~2.44M
bits of key complexity for full Unicode). Full derivation: docs/HYPERWEBSTER.md.

### Architecture: Eleven Faces

Sovereign capability domains, each named after a Library-of-Alexandria-
associated historical figure, each running its own local "SMNNIP Instance
Engine" conservation verifier: Pharos (system health/message bus),
Alexandria (visual/rendering), Anaximander (spatial/geolocation),
Archimedes (math/physics/signal — the ValaQuenta-facing one), Aulë
(diagnostics/audit), Callimachus (info architecture/HyperWebster corpus/
